n we're going to throw in some  already sliced up mushrooms  they will skinny down  they will sweat down on their own in the  sauce  and we're gonna add salt and pepper  about two teaspoons of salt  especially if you bought a chicken that  was not  seasoned you want to add some good  flavor  and a teaspoon of pepper to give it some  heat  and we're going to stir this around and  are you ready here's where things get  really easy and fun we're going to take  two 28 ounce cans  of fire roasted chopped tomatoes  into the pot  into the pot and to give it great  flavor we're going to add my favorite  that i use with everything the rayos  arabiata sauce which has got a lot of  spice and heat to it  so good right into the pot we're gonna  stir this around  and into the pot goes the chicken  we're gonna let it cook for about an  hour  just to get all the flavors to melt  together ready here we go  [Music]  and so now this is my favorite part  about having a garden out back  is i came out here and clipped some  rosemary oregano and basil to throw  into the chicken cacciatore  [Music]  and that's it everybody so easy  happy making whatever it is you're  making while you're home  this pairs nicely with a great glass of  red  italian wine served with a baguette  sliced up so you can dip into the sauce  eat your chicken  and no stress have a wonderful holiday  season everyone and remember  spread love like butter oh we're all  salivating in the studio  i like that one i think i can do that  one check out nanny bubby's kitchen and  garden on social media  and online at nannybubby.com we also  want to thank chapman automotive for  sponsoring this segment rocky
 

